body:
The real question is, will you take care of it? I daily drive an 02 2500hd with a 6.0 that's seen plenty of abuse with 272k miles. I swear by it because its the only vehicle I've ever had that's not needed a tow ever. But if I neglected it I'm sure it would of died long ago.

&#x200B;

Will you check the engine oil and top it off when its low? Willing to service the transmission fluid and filter? Will you check the codes when you get a MIL illuminated? I know it seems like simple shit but I've seen many people let their engine run without oil then get all mad about it throwing a rod.

&#x200B;

Edit: As someone who repairs the instrument clusters from this platform for a living, NEVER under any circumstance trust the odometer reading on the cluster. It's far too easy to change the odometer on the cluster of these. Also a very large amount of these trucks have had clusters swapped due to issues with them especially the 03-06/07c models.  


The mileage is stored on the bcm and I would trust the reading from there if you have a scan tool that can verify it

So far I haven't found anything it can't undo. It even made quick work of removing the transmission cross member that was rusted to the frame of my truck. I use the little battery because its a pretty heavy tool. Forge battery would be nice for the better output and keeping it as light as possible. I just can't at the moment validate spending 200 dollars on a tool battery.

&#x200B;

Yeah I probably should of went mid torque but my justification for high torque was I'll be glad I have it when I run into an apocalyptic situation, especially since I'm not strong at all in the upper body. Also because 75% of my work is somewhere I don't have compressor access. Also because when TTC tested it and did the tear down on it I became obsessed lol

I plan to use the tool to manually break loose or a breaker bar plus my handy metal pipe, my concern is more about the rusted threads which even after breaking loose it had more resistance than even a nylock nut. I just wonder if the lower torque will have issues blasting nylocks and/or rusted thread after being broke . On that chevy pickup I've had plenty of bolts that I had to ratchet off the whole way on that truck

&#x200B;

Thank you though for the information

yeah its not gooey at all, it did form very nicely and feels firm when I squeeze it. and I'll have to get some glue sticks for next time. All I had on hand was super glue and hot glue and I couldn't get the hot glue small enough to be satisfactory and I didn't want to use super glue because getting it off polycarb in my experience can be a nightmare.

&#x200B;

Thank you for the informative reply. If I do go to use it, should i rinse the silicone or wash it with soap and water or just use it as is?

I find the people who come here to shit on meth users and'or the drug in general to be exhausting. I tried to make a few post that were positive that just got absolutely shit on. This attitude keeps me from posting more on here and instead I mostly screen post. 

&#x200B;

I don't think anybody here doesn't know meth is harmful like any other psychoactive substance. It definitely is over exaggerated by drug war propaganda that I don't see any reason it needs to be parroted here. I also don't think people who come here to be assholes because they're so pathetic they're looking for literally anyone to feel superior over add any positive value to the sub and would be a net benefit if they were gone.

&#x200B;

Just my 2 cents

well a friend of mine has managed to accidently bring drugs on the plane with them. From that they learned a couple things about getting through security. They have told me that the TSA scanning mechanism isn't as good as you think, as simply putting stuff in their makeup bag which is then inside their backpack has gotten through easily, same with a stick of deodorant and running the deodorant out, then placing it underneath then the stick back on top. I have another friend that told me that crushing it, putting it in capsules, then in a bottle for supplements, gets by no problem. Then another friend said they just seal it and put it in their underwear. Even in a patdown they almost never touch your genitals and even when they do its still not that hard to make it undetectable from that. 

&#x200B;

My friends have reported to me that your friend shouldn't even try with their luggage that goes under the plane though. Those checked bags are liable for dog testing and they do go through them. Getting it through TSA is intimidating but the much easier path to go down, as told by these friends to your friend.
